    "extract": "The Ruffinihaus (from German: \"Ruffini House\") is a group of three houses (also known as Ruffinihäuser) on the Rindermarkt (\"cattle market\") in the Old Town of Munich, Bavaria. It was built by Gabriel von Seidl from 1903 to 1905 and is named after the Ruffiniturm (\"Ruffini tower\", demolished in 1808), which in turn was named after Johann Baptista Ruffini. The Ruffiniturm formed the original Sendlinger Tor (\"Sendlinger gate\") and thus was part of Munich's first city wall. \nThe Ruffinihaus is a three-sided house that borders Sendlinger and Pettenbeck streets. The Ruffinihaus stands on what was the fluvial terrace of the first medieval fortification's moat, as can still be seen today when viewe",
